# SwiftFormat configuration for district-macos.
#
# The same options as district-ios and district-core-swift, so code moved between the
# three repositories formats identically. Deliberately minimal: the default rule set,
# with only the options that pin house style so `swiftformat --lint` in CI is
# reproducible.
#
# ⚠️ RUN `swiftformat .` FROM THE PROJECT ROOT (the directory holding this file).
# The tool discovers this file by walking up from each input path.
#
# CI runs `swiftformat --lint .` (SwiftFormat 0.63.0), which formats nothing and exits
# non-zero on any file that would change.

# ⚠️ MUST TRACK the Swift that Xcode 26.3 ships (6.2) and the swift image in the
# workflow. A version newer than the toolchain makes the formatter emit code the
# compiler rejects; older, and it silently skips modernisation rules.
--swiftversion 6.2

--indent 4
--maxwidth 120
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--wrapcollections before-first
--closingparen balanced
# ⚠️ `collections-only`, NOT the `always` default. `always` also adds a trailing comma to
# function argument lists, which is Swift 6.1+ syntax; collections have taken one since
# Swift 1.
--trailing-commas collections-only
--trimwhitespace always
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--self remove
--importgrouping alpha

# Generated and vendored trees. All are gitignored, but --lint would still walk them.
--exclude .build,**/.build,DerivedData,**/DerivedData,SourcePackages,*.xcodeproj

# ⚠️ `redundantInit` OFF, as in district-ios: it has historically got `map(Foo.init)`
# wrong inside result-builder bodies.
--disable redundantInit
